This is a PUBLIC BETA program, meaning that it is

                     EXTREMELY DANGEROUS!!!!!

If you do not read the docs and make full backups before testing
this program, you're taking your BBS's sanity into your own
hands!

I appreciate the help that all the kindly DLG sysops out there
have given me, but if you do not take to heart that this software
can do serious damage and thus take preventative measures, I
really don't want you to test this software.  Wait until version
1.0 is released.  You'll be happy and I won't have to waste my
time telling you "I told you so."

On the other hand, if you wish to help out in the testing of this
program, you'll have my thanks, the chance to test some possibly
excellent software ahead of time, and have a chance to shape the
direction it takes over the development cycle.

I would STRONGLY suggest that you read the history file AND the
release notes.  These two files contain any information detailing
new features and changes, plus explain at length any
behind-the-scenes action taking place. There are no indications
of this in the manual, other than the updating of information,
but that updating is not evident unless you're a careful reader.

Thank you for taking the time for reading this.  Get those tape
drives cranking, and welcome to the next level :-)

